('applied-linux-a04-l2', 9, 2, 'Networking, DNS, ports, and HTTPS', 'orange', 'Separate name resolution, routing, listening ports, and HTTP/TLS evidence.', 'Check the listening service', '8 min', 'DNS maps names to addresses; routes select next hops; sockets show listeners; HTTPS adds certificate and hostname checks. These checks are separate.', 'The host resolves correctly but the API is listening on 8443 while another virtual service occupies 443. Distinguish port selection from DNS and app health.', '[{"id":"a04-2-task-1","title":"Inspect listening training ports.","description":"Inspect listening training ports.","hint":"First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","hints":["First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","Use the ip addr capability introduced for this lesson to inspect or change the training state.","For this task, start with: ip addr — inspect listening training ports.."],"feedback":"Listening socket state is read.","expectedOutcome":"Listening socket state is read."},{"id":"a04-2-task-2","title":"Compare the app port with the requested address.","description":"Compare the app port with the requested address.","hint":"First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","hints":["First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","Use the ip route capability introduced for this lesson to inspect or change the training state.","For this task, start with: ip route — compare the app port with the requested address.."],"feedback":"Service and request ports are separated.","expectedOutcome":"Service and request ports are separated."},{"id":"a04-2-task-3","title":"Test the appropriate endpoint and classify the response.","description":"Test the appropriate endpoint and classify the response.","hint":"First iden