('sre-operations-b01-l2', 16, 2, 'Access, metrics, and baselines', 'mint', 'Establish scope, compare transaction signals, and compute a baseline.', 'Investigate a transaction drop', '8 min', 'Metric values depend on resource, statistic, period, timezone, filters, and source. The three dashboard names and datasets are fictional training fixtures.', 'Compare the same time window for WEB-1, WEB-2, and WEB-3. Fixtures include Monday/Wednesday 9 AM and monthly patterns; recurrence is not proof of harmlessness.', '[{"id":"b01-2-task-1","title":"Compare attempts, successes, failures, and logs for same window.","description":"Compare attempts, successes, failures, and logs for same window.","hint":"First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","hints":["First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","Use the training dashboards capability introduced for this lesson to inspect or change the training state.","For this task, start with: training dashboards — compare attempts, successes, failures, and logs for same window.."],"feedback":"Resources and time windows align.","expectedOutcome":"Resources and time windows align."},{"id":"b01-2-task-2","title":"Calculate the supplied drop/success rate.","description":"Calculate the supplied drop/success rate.","hint":"First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","hints":["First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","Use the metric definitions capability introduced for this lesson to inspect or change the training state.","For this task, start with: metric definitions — calculate the supplied drop/success rate.."],"feedback":"Calculation is correct.","expectedOutcome":"Calculation is correct."},{"id":"b01-2-task-3","title":"Distinguish reduced demand, failed processing, and missing