('sre-operations-b01-l3', 16, 3, 'Access, metrics, and baselines', 'mint', 'Establish scope, compare transaction signals, and compute a baseline.', 'Calculate a baseline and buffer', '8 min', 'Metric values depend on resource, statistic, period, timezone, filters, and source. The three dashboard names and datasets are fictional training fixtures.', 'Use comparable historical periods and statistics. Explain missing samples and the limits of a three-month comparison.', '[{"id":"b01-3-task-1","title":"Select comparable resources, periods, and statistic.","description":"Select comparable resources, periods, and statistic.","hint":"First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","hints":["First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","Use the training dashboards capability introduced for this lesson to inspect or change the training state.","For this task, start with: training dashboards — select comparable resources, periods, and statistic.."],"feedback":"Dataset selection is defensible.","expectedOutcome":"Dataset selection is defensible."},{"id":"b01-3-task-2","title":"Calculate a baseline from available samples.","description":"Calculate a baseline from available samples.","hint":"First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","hints":["First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","Use the metric definitions capability introduced for this lesson to inspect or change the training state.","For this task, start with: metric definitions — calculate a baseline from available samples.."],"feedback":"Baseline arithmetic is correct.","expectedOutcome":"Baseline arithmetic is correct."},{"id":"b01-3-task-3","title":"Distinguish percentage-point buffer from relative percentage and note gaps.","description":"Distinguish percenta