('sre-operations-b03-l1', 18, 1, 'Request tracing, routing, and API simulators', 'purple', 'Trace fictional request paths and diagnose routing evidence.', 'Trace a request across services', '8 min', 'The trace and route data are training fixtures. AFOD, GW2, ECPay, DPU, MPI proxy, and similar terms are not assigned meanings unless confirmed by supplied evidence.', 'Follow one correlation ID through a fictional kiosk, API Core, and ECS-hosted QR service. Missing evidence must remain missing; a QR response does not prove cash-in completion.', '[{"id":"b03-1-task-1","title":"Inspect timestamps and outbound calls for the correlation ID.","description":"Inspect timestamps and outbound calls for the correlation ID.","hint":"First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","hints":["First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","Use the trace viewer capability introduced for this lesson to inspect or change the training state.","For this task, start with: trace viewer — inspect timestamps and outbound calls for the correlation id.."],"feedback":"Correlation ID remains consistent.","expectedOutcome":"Correlation ID remains consistent."},{"id":"b03-1-task-2","title":"Compare responses and missing stage entries.","description":"Compare responses and missing stage entries.","hint":"First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","hints":["First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","Use the routing dashboard capability introduced for this lesson to inspect or change the training state.","For this task, start with: routing dashboard — compare responses and missing stage entries.."],"feedback":"Evidence path and gap are identified.","expectedOutcome":"Evidence path and gap are identified."},{"id":"b03-1-task-3","title":"Explain pr