('sre-operations-b04-l1', 19, 1, 'Vulnerability findings and security events', 'orange', 'Separate raw security evidence from interpretation and confidence.', 'Review a vulnerability finding', '8 min', 'Security findings and event rules are fictional training records. An empty findings view does not establish scan coverage.', 'Inspect fictional Inspector-style EC2, ECR, and Lambda findings with package, version, severity, scan time, coverage, fix, and owner.', '[{"id":"b04-1-task-1","title":"Compare resource type and identity.","description":"Compare resource type and identity.","hint":"First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","hints":["First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","Use the findings dashboard capability introduced for this lesson to inspect or change the training state.","For this task, start with: findings dashboard — compare resource type and identity.."],"feedback":"Resource scope is exact.","expectedOutcome":"Resource scope is exact."},{"id":"b04-1-task-2","title":"Record package/version/severity/scan time/coverage/recommended fix.","description":"Record package/version/severity/scan time/coverage/recommended fix.","hint":"First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","hints":["First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","Use the event viewer capability introduced for this lesson to inspect or change the training state.","For this task, start with: event viewer — record package/version/severity/scan time/coverage/recommended fix.."],"feedback":"Coverage and recommendation are captured.","expectedOutcome":"Coverage and recommendation are captured."},{"id":"b04-1-task-3","title":"Identify fictional owner and explain what finding alone does not prove.","description":"Identify fictional owne