('sre-operations-b04-l2', 19, 2, 'Vulnerability findings and security events', 'orange', 'Separate raw security evidence from interpretation and confidence.', 'Understand a Wazuh-style event', '8 min', 'Security findings and event rules are fictional training records. An empty findings view does not establish scan coverage.', 'Follow a raw event through collection, decoder, matching rule, endpoint, severity, storage, and display.', '[{"id":"b04-2-task-1","title":"Read the raw event and extracted fields.","description":"Read the raw event and extracted fields.","hint":"First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","hints":["First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","Use the findings dashboard capability introduced for this lesson to inspect or change the training state.","For this task, start with: findings dashboard — read the raw event and extracted fields.."],"feedback":"Raw fields are preserved.","expectedOutcome":"Raw fields are preserved."},{"id":"b04-2-task-2","title":"Identify decoder/rule and endpoint/time.","description":"Identify decoder/rule and endpoint/time.","hint":"First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","hints":["First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would distinguish the possible causes.","Use the event viewer capability introduced for this lesson to inspect or change the training state.","For this task, start with: event viewer — identify decoder/rule and endpoint/time.."],"feedback":"Rule and decoder are correctly linked.","expectedOutcome":"Rule and decoder are correctly linked."},{"id":"b04-2-task-3","title":"Separate raw facts from rule-assigned interpretation.","description":"Separate raw facts from rule-assigned interpretation.","hint":"First identify the resource, time scope, and observable evidence that would d